<!--
# Hello Lambda

Deploys `examples/bsx_site` as an http-only AWS Lambda (behind an API Gateway URL,
no custom domain). The generic `beet` binary is packaged as a `provided.al2023`
function and reads the site from an S3 bucket at request time (the zip's
`bootstrap` script launches it with `--repo=s3://<bucket> --server=http`, since
the lambda runtime offers no argv), so a site change re-publishes by re-running
`sync` with no redeploy.

## Usage

    beet --main=examples/infra/lambda.bsx validate
    beet --main=examples/infra/lambda.bsx deploy
    beet --main=examples/infra/lambda.bsx sync
    beet --main=examples/infra/lambda.bsx watch
    beet --main=examples/infra/lambda.bsx destroy --force

A one-shot `CliServer` root whose `CallOnReady` fires the CLI request on load, with
the `Router` as its dispatch child. `<Stack app_name="lambda">` is the resource
identity every block and verb beneath it resolves by ancestry, and `<DeployRoutes/>`
adds the standard IaC verb routes (validate/plan/apply/...) to it. Each verb below is
a child-sequenced `<Route path=".." {ExchangeSequence}>`: its block and actions are
direct children of the route and the sequence runs them in order.

Live deploy needs AWS credentials in the environment, plus `tofu`,
`cargo-zigbuild` and `zip`.
-->
<CliServer {CallOnReady}>
<Router {(RequestLogger, HelpHandler)}>
	<CrateCheck features={["infra", "extra"]}/>
	<Stack app_name="lambda">
		<DeployRoutes/>
		<Route path="deploy" {ExchangeSequence}>
			<!-- the block + its build artifact share one entity (the deploy pairs them) -->
			<LambdaSiteBlock features="lambda,aws_sdk"/>
			<S3BucketBlock label="app" deploy_versioned=false/>
			<!-- the bucket first, so the site is in place before the function that
			     serves it exists -->
			<TofuApply layer="storage"/>
			<SiteSync/>
			<TofuApply/>
			<!-- the rollout is quick, so tail briefly then exit -->
			<LambdaWatch timeout="30s"/>
		</Route>
		<Route path="sync" {ExchangeSequence}>
			<SiteSync/>
		</Route>
		<Route path="watch" {ExchangeSequence}>
			<LambdaWatch/>
		</Route>
	</Stack>
</Router>
</CliServer>
